    "id": "distribute-pilot18",
    "language": "[0]In this scenario, let's say that both of our strikers are blocked. If both of our strikers are blocked, we should not risk a forward pass straight to our opponent. In this case, we should pick either of our supporting players beneath us or to the right or left of us, and pa- and lay the ball off to them. [1]Then...[2][3][4][5] Then, we can move to a supporting[6] position up here, higher up the field, where we can receive the ball and move forward later on.",
